The '''T-47 airspeeder''', also known as the '''T-47 light airspeeder''', was a craft manufactured by [[Incom Corporation]]. They were modified by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] into [[snowspeeder]]s.

==Characteristics==
{{Quote|No, no, not the T-47! I can fly anything, but that doesn't mean I want to. Piloting the T-47 is like steering a block of wood.|Poe Dameron|<ref name="RebelFiles" />}}
[[File:Luke_crashed_snowspeeder.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Luke salvaging equipment from his crashed snowspeeder on Hoth.]]
The T-47 airspeeder, also known as the T-47 light airspeeder,<ref name="Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref> was a model of low-altitude vehicle manufactured by [[Incom Corporation]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The vessel was designed for civilian usage and saw use hauling sewage,<ref name="Part IV" /> but they would go onto see service as military craft. All the same, the vessel was not a particularly maneuverable craft, to the extent that [[Resistance pilot]] [[Poe Dameron]]&mdash;despite saying that he could, if needed, fly the ship&mdash;compared piloting a T-47 to trying to steer "a block of wood."<ref name="RebelFiles" />

A small, wedge-shaped vehicle, the T-47 was a two-person craft crewed by a [[pilot]] and a rear-facing tailgunner,<ref name="ESB" /> with a top speed of 1,100 [[Kilometer per hour|kph]].<ref name="Encyc" /> At least in the case of its modified, military form, it had two forward-facing heavy [[laser cannon]]s and a [[Magnetic harpoon|harpoon cannon]] placed in the rear and manned by the tailgunner.<ref name="ESB" />

==History==
{{Quote|Yeah, well, we're not soldiers. Those speeders are for hauling sewage.|Sully Stark|<ref name="Part IV" />}}
In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="OBK Timeline">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}} states that ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' is set ten [[Standard year|years]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]]. Therefore, ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' must be set in [[9 BBY]].</ref> T-47s were used to haul sewage but saw use by the [[Hidden Path]]. When [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Tala Durith]] [[Rescue of Princess Leia (9 BBY)|rescued]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[Sully Stark]], and [[Wade Resselian]] helped them escape from [[Fortress Inquisitorius]] by strafing the stronghold's landing platform in their T-47s. However, [[Reva Sevander]] threw an explosive using [[the Force]] at Resselian's airspeeder which caused it to explode, killing him.<ref name="Part IV" />

[[File:T47Airspeeder-SWL2024update.png|thumb|300px|right|A trio of T-47s cripple an Imperial AT-AT on Sullust.]]
During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the [[Partisans]] had access to T-47s during their [[Jedha insurgency|insurgency]] on [[Jedha]].<ref name="SW 38" /> During the [[Battle of Hoth]], Rebel Alliance snowspeeders used tow cables to disable [[All Terrain Armored Transport]] (AT-AT) [[walker]]s by firing the tow cable and chasing it out around the walker's legs, stopping its locomotion and immobilizing the walker.<ref name="swe" /> At some point, three T-47s attacked and crippled an AT-AT on [[Sullust]].<ref name="SWL Update">{{Asmodee|subdomain=cdn.svc|domain=net|url=production-amgcom/uploads/2025/04/DOC13_RebelAlliance_Units.pdf|text=''Star Wars: Legion'' Rebel Alliance Command Cards (PDF)}}</ref>

{{Veh-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The T-47 airspeeder first appeared in the [[1980]] film [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']].<ref name="ESB" />

